# The maverick commit this repository builds its SDK and packaging tools from.
#
# CI checks out maverick at exactly this SHA, builds mav-connector-sdk and mav-connector-tool from
# it, and runs the deep validation path against them. Pinning is the point: an unpinned checkout
# means a connector that passed CI yesterday can fail today for a reason nobody changed here, and a
# floating SDK means the artifacts this repo signs were built against something nobody recorded.
#
# Bumping it is a deliberate commit: change the SHA, run the full local validation against that
# checkout, and say in the commit message what in maverick made the bump necessary.
